## Monorepo Layout: Simulation & RL Agent Separation

The codebase follows the monorepo architecture described in `skills/gymnasium-env/references/structure.md`:

```
{{ project_name }}/
├── pyproject.toml         # Root workspace manifest (members = ["packages/*"])
├── justfile               # Monorepo tasks orchestrator
├── AGENTS.md              # Agent operational guidance
├── assets/                # Centralized assets (fonts, textures, audio)
├── packages/
│   ├── env/               # 👈 Simulation environment package ({{ package_name }}-env)
│   │   ├── pyproject.toml
│   │   ├── src/{{ package_name }}_env/
│   │   │   ├── core/      # PhysicsState with __slots__, deterministic transitions
│   │   │   ├── env/       # CustomEnv (gym.Env) and reward shaping
│   │   │   ├── engine/    # RaylibRenderer (isolated hardware drawing)
│   │   │   └── cli.py     # Fire CLI (play, test_env)
│   │   └── tests/         # Physics properties, reward invariants, Farama check_env
│   └── agents/            # 👈 RL training and evaluation package ({{ package_name }}-agents)
│       ├── pyproject.toml # Depends on {{ package_name }}-env via { workspace = true }
│       ├── src/{{ package_name }}_agents/
│       │   ├── agent/     # Agent Protocol, RandomAgent, HeuristicAgent
│       │   ├── eval/      # Multi-seed evaluator and metrics report
│       │   ├── training/  # Training loop & sweep harness
│       │   └── cli.py     # Fire CLI (eval, train)
│       └── tests/         # Policy decisions and evaluation tests
```

### Critical Architectural Invariants

1. **Strict Decoupling of Simulation & Agents:**
   - The simulation package (`packages/env`) **never** imports from the agents package (`packages/agents`).
   - The agents package interacts with the simulation purely via standard Gymnasium interfaces (`gym.Env`).
2. **Headless Execution:**
   - Simulation logic (`core/`, `env/`) and training loops **must never** import Raylib or open graphical windows.
   - All visual rendering in `engine/renderer.py` is isolated and only triggered when `render_mode="human"`.
3. **Reset Signature & Determinism:**
   - `reset(seed=None, options=None) -> tuple[ObsType, dict[str, Any]]`
   - Must call `super().reset(seed=seed)` to initialize `self.np_random`.
   - Identical seeds must produce identical initial states and trajectories.
4. **Step Signature:**
   - `step(action) -> tuple[ObsType, float, bool, bool, dict[str, Any]]`
   - Returning `(observation, reward, terminated, truncated, info)`.
   - Never combine `terminated` and `truncated`.
5. **Reward Engineering:**
   - Reward calculations live in pure functions in `packages/env/src/{{ package_name }}_env/env/reward.py`.
   - Rewards must be provably bounded.

